<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · song</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sansoen Phra Barami</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">tune chosen <a href="/years/1871">1871</a>; sheet music printed <a href="/years/1888">1888</a>; words <a href="/years/1886">1886</a>, revised <a href="/years/1914">1914</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as สรรเสริญพระบารมี</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">&quot;Sansoen Phra Barami&quot; (&quot;Praise the King&quot;) is the royal anthem of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thailand">Thailand</a>, and before 1932 it served as the de facto national anthem of Siam. Its history begins in the reign of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongkut">Mongkut</a>.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>&quot;<b>Sansoen Phra Barami</b>&quot; (&quot;Praise the King&quot;) is the royal anthem of Thailand, and before 1932 it served as the de facto national anthem of Siam.</blockquote><a href="/songs/sansoen-phra-barami">Sansoen Phra Barami</a></li><li><blockquote>Before 1932 the royal anthem &quot;<b>Sansoen Phra Barami</b>&quot; served as Siam's anthem in fact.</blockquote><a href="/songs/thai-national-anthem">Thai National Anthem</a></li></ul></section>
